# Declared frame pairs of the hand-derived frame literals (plan 07-02, D-21): one line per pair,
#   <idA> <idB> <x> <y> <w> <h> <count>
# idA and idB are ids of data/expected/video-frames.ids; x y w h is the rectangle in plane positions (x 0..158, y 0..95);
# count is the number of positions at which the two planes differ. The video step (token video-frame-pair-region) requires
# that the planes differ at exactly count positions and that every differing position lies inside the rectangle, so a response
# frame that changes anything outside its declared region, or fewer or more positions than derived, cannot be registered.
# The counts are derived by hand in docs/video/demo-lamp-tone-1-derivation.md section (e): 64 positions per lit lamp that the other frame shows unlit.
# Plan 08-03 adds the two pairs of the program ivs-diag-stic-2, derived by hand in docs/video/diag-stic-2-derivation.md sections (b) and (e): a frame with an unknown region (F-M7) is never paired.
F-S1 F-S2 48 32 64 8 128
F-S1 F-S3 48 32 64 8 256
F-S2 F-S3 48 32 64 8 128
F-S1 F-S4 48 56 64 8 64
F-S1 F-S5 48 32 64 32 192
F-S1 F-S6 48 32 64 32 384
F-S5 F-S6 48 32 64 32 320
F-M0 F-M1 150 90 9 6 38
F-M0 F-M4 0 0 159 96 2012
